Article 16

1. The Regional Government through the Office/UPTD is obliged to carry out economic empowerment for victims of acts of violence, exploitation and neglect.

(2) Forms of empowerment of victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), include:
a. providing the necessary needs for entrepreneurship training for victims of acts of violence, in order to increase knowledge, attitudes, and business skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic enterprises;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop the businesses of victims of acts of violence;
e. seeking the provision of capital for victims of acts of violence; and f. expanding access to information and promoting the products of victims of acts of violence.

Article 18

(1i The Regional Government establishes partnerships with the business community for support in the implementation of protection for women and children in the regional area.

2. Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1), is carried out through: a. notification of information on employment opportunities for women victims of acts of violence;
b. education and training for women victims of acts of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; and d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of acts of violence. (3) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2], shall be set forth in the form of a cooperation agreement.

CHAPTER XII

INVESTIGATION

Article 23 (1) In addition to general investigating officers, investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children in this Regional Regulation may also be carried out by Civil Servant Investigators whose appointment is in accordance with laws and regulations. with Regulation (21 Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1), are authorized to:
a. receive reports or complaints from a person regarding the existence of criminal acts of violence against women and children;
b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct an examination; c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identity;
d. seize objects and/or letters; e. take fingerprints and photograph a person; f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in experts needed in connection with the examination of the case;
h. cease investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the public prosecutor, the suspect or their family; and/or i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be accounted for.
3. Investigators as referred to in paragraph (2), shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through the Investigating Officer of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code. v;
.

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

REGENT OF EAST BARITO,

Considering:
a. that women and children with their dignity have the right to be protected from various acts of violence, exploitation, and discrimination that marginalize and degrade their dignity as human beings;
b. that negative behavior and actions that may result in women and children being in a position of pressure or powerlessness in the scope of social community, or in the scope of legal processes should be given special treatment that maintains the stability of their soul and spirit to remain able to carry out their lives in social interaction;
c. that the Regional Government is obliged to provide protection for women and children;
d. Bearing in Mind 1. 2.
3. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children;

